00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:52.620
Sure. The suits that we're running today were future lunar and Mars surface suits.

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:58.110
Test beds actually. We're trying to take and incorporate some changes into the suits that

00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:59.530
they didn't have during the Apollo days.

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:04.660
which will enable them to be able to walk on the moon's surface rather than hop, as they did before.

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:09.480
The hopping, while worked better than walking, was fatiguing for the astronaut.

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:12.140
It was very hard on the calves and the ankles.

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:18.890
So in order to take and alleviate that, we've incorporated bearings into the hips and into the ankles of these suits

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:22.090
to allow more freedom of movement.

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:27.700
So we have a bearing here, here, and here, which allows for good freedom of movement.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:29.900
Another thing that they don't have that they didn't have

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.200
